cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Code for: Calibration, Conformal Prediction and Selective Automation for Bearing Fault Diagnosis: From Artificial to Real Damage"
authors:
  - given-names: Yam
    family-names: Malla
    email: yammalla09@gmail.com
  - given-names: Bhuwan
    family-names: Karki
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/amritmalla/bearing-uq-artificial-to-real"
abstract: >-
  Code and results for a study of whether calibrated confidence in bearing fault diagnosis survives the shift
  from artificially made faults to real damage on the Paderborn bearing dataset: Random Forest, SVM and XGBoost
  on envelope-spectrum features and a 1D-CNN on raw vibration, with bearing-level splits, temperature scaling,
  isotonic regression, split conformal prediction and selective automation.
keywords:
  - bearing fault diagnosis
  - calibration
  - conformal prediction
  - selective classification
  - domain shift
  - Paderborn bearing dataset
